oris-trace 1
# A free tree block of at most 256 bytes goes to the small free list, not the red-black
# tree. A 1000-byte block shrunk in place to 100 bytes (112 with its rounding) leaves its
# tail free; an 860-byte request takes that tail, so the small block now sits between two
# live ones. Freed, it is the most-recently-freed block; the next free flushes it to the
# small list (list+); freeing its neighbour coalesces it away (list-).
alloc h0 1000
alloc h1 300
realloc h0 100
alloc h2 860
free h0
free h1
free h2
purge
